@meowgorithm done on both counts:

**Rebase** — rebased onto `main` (post-#3345) rather than merging; the branch now carries only this PR's commits and the stack note is gone from the description. One reconciliation was needed: #3345's review added the filter that keeps channel events out of the shared `SubscribeEvents` fan-out, deferring delivery wiring to this PR. Delivery now flows through a channel-only `SubscribeChannelEvents` — the backend router consumes it directly, and each app scopes its own subscription to the servers its workspace declares and opted in, so the cross-workspace leak stays closed (`e0d07e2f`).

**Reaping** — good push; as written the column was effectively write-only and never cleared. It now has a full lifecycle (`b32e9e71`): the coordinator reconciles the binding on every turn — a channel-originated turn (re)binds the session (newest push wins), a local turn clears it (a session the user takes over is no longer channel-driven), and the column is dropped with the session row on delete. So there's no separate lifetime and no reaper pass needed; the binding can't outlive the session or go stale past the next turn. This also fixed a gap where only the in-process TUI persisted the binding — the coordinator is shared by both the in-process and server paths, so client/server now records it too. Lifecycle covered by `TestSyncSessionChannelLifecycle`.

Heads-up on one addition folded in with the rebase: **`channel_enabled`** (`eb71820b`), ported from joestump-agent/crush#181 where we've been running it on the fork.

It's a per-server config boolean that opts an MCP server into the channel system persistently from `crush.json`, instead of requiring `--channels <name>` on every launch:

```json
{
  "mcp": {
    "webhook": {
      "type": "http",
      "url": "https://example.com/mcp",
      "channel_enabled": true
    }
  }
}
```

The two sources are ORed by a single `ChannelOptIn` helper used at every gate site (session creation, renewal, OAuth reconnect, app event scoping, backend routing), so either works and they compose. It doesn't bypass the capability gate — the server must still declare `claude/channel` — and merely listing a server under `mcp` is still not enough, so the "listed is not enabled" model holds. schema.json is regenerated; user-facing docs land with the README section in part 3/3. Covered by `TestChannelOptIn` and `TestRouteChannelMessage_ConfigEnabled`.

