- `mcp-remote` stdio hangs consistently (the 2-minute timeout in this issue)
- The `mcp-remote` version directory bug you mentioned (`~/.mcp-auth/mcp-remote-{version}`) — we hit that too when testing pinned vs unpinned versions

Our workaround was similar but used the HTTP transport with a pre-obtained Bearer token instead of `oauth: true`:

```json
{
  "mcp": {
    "jira": {
      "type": "http",
      "url": "https://mcp.atlassian.com/v1/mcp/authv2",
      "headers": {
        "Authorization": "Bearer $(jira-mcp-token.sh)"
      },
      "timeout": 30
    }
  }
}
```

Where `jira-mcp-token.sh` reads the cached token from `~/.mcp-auth`. This requires re-running `npx -y mcp-remote@0.1.38 https://mcp.atlassian.com/v1/mcp/authv2` every ~8 hours to refresh the token, which is clunky but works.

