Following up on this with a concrete breakdown of the local vs server discrepancy:

In `internal/backend/agent.go` (server mode), `SetMainAgent` enforces:
```go
if ws.AgentCoordinator.IsBusy() {
    return ErrAgentBusy
}
return ws.AgentCoordinator.SetMainAgent(agentID)
```

However, in `internal/workspace/app_workspace.go` (local mode), `AgentSetMain` currently lacks this check:
```go
func (w *AppWorkspace) AgentSetMain(agentID string) error {
    if w.app.AgentCoordinator == nil {
        return errors.New("agent coordinator not initialized")
    }
    // Missing: w.app.AgentCoordinator.IsBusy() check
    return w.app.AgentCoordinator.SetMainAgent(agentID)
}
```

Adding the busy check in `AppWorkspace.AgentSetMain` aligns local mode with the server mode contract and prevents mid-run agent switching when UI state or caching diverges.

